  "body": "https://webidl.spec.whatwg.org/#idl-grammar describes the grammar symbols in terms of fonts, which isn't really accessible. We should find some other way of talking about them.\r\n\r\nIt might be sufficient to say something like:\r\n\r\n> These are the generic terminal symbols: [regular expression symbols here]. The other terminal symbols listed in this section are the specific terminal symbols.\r\n\r\n(Non-terminals starting with an uppercase character seems somewhat fine. Although even that isn't the epitome of accessibility.)",
